  "tagline": "Open-source columnar OLAP database known for very fast aggregations over billions of rows.",
  "description": "ClickHouse is a column-oriented SQL database built for real-time analytics: MergeTree tables sort and compress data on disk, and a vectorized engine scans billions of rows per second per server. It shines on append-heavy event, log, observability and product-analytics data, with materialized views, TTLs, skip indexes, a native JSON type and vector and text indexes. It can run as a single binary, a sharded self-managed cluster or ClickHouse Cloud with storage on S3. Updates, deletes and complex multi-way joins have improved a lot but remain weaker than in a classic warehouse.",
